title: 'fix(grandpa): do not serve warp proofs from an incomplete list of authority set changes'
doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Two fixes for nodes that warp synced and then serve warp proofs.

      Warp proof generation now fails with `MissingData` when the node has a header gap and the
      requested proof starts below the end of that gap. The authority set changes of the blocks
      in the gap are only recorded when gap sync imports them. Until then the node answered with
      an empty proof, with a proof that ended early but was marked as finished and verified, or
      with a proof that failed verification at the client.

      GRANDPA block import now records the authority set change enacted by a block that is
      imported with state. When the target of a warp sync was itself an authority set change
      block, that change was never recorded, the list kept a hole after gap sync, and the node
      served warp proofs that clients rejected with `bad justification`.

      No API change.
  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      A node that is still downloading block history after warp sync now refuses warp proof
      requests that depend on that history, with `Missing required data`, until the download is
      complete.
crates:
  - name: sc-consensus-grandpa
    bump: patch
